WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.821
Cross joins make cardinality especially visible
because the multiplication is direct Two

00:00:06.847 --> 00:00:11.574
rows crossed with three rows create six result rows
One hundred by

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.811
one hundred creates ten thousand Ten thousand by ten
thousand creates one

00:00:16.837 --> 00:00:22.622
hundred million This does not mean CROSS JOIN is bad
It

00:00:22.635 --> 00:00:28.296
means the result size should be intentional For
example building every

00:00:28.323 --> 00:00:31.507
department and every appointment slot can be exactly
what you need to

00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:37.141
find missing schedule assignments But crossing two
large transaction tables would usually

00:00:37.154 --> 00:00:43.067
be a serious mistake The same multiplication idea
appears less obviously

00:00:43.093 --> 00:00:46.317
in ordinary joins when both sides can have several
matches for the

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:51.543
same key That is why understanding cardinality is
essential before we move

00:00:51.557 --> 00:00:57.247
into multi-table analytical joins Whenever a result
suddenly contains

00:00:57.273 --> 00:01:01.825
far more rows than expected ask whether you have
accidentally created combinations

00:01:01.839 --> 00:01:03.576
between multiple detail rows
